>> title: White Sandwich Bread
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, yeast, milk, oven, sandwich
>> counters: Bakery, Deli
>> aka: white bread, sandwich loaf, pullman loaf
>> servings: 12
>> time: 3 hr
>> slack: forgiving — an hour rising or ninety minutes makes very little difference and the dough is judged by doubling; the loaf comes out at 200°F at the centre, and one pulled early collapses along the sides in the tin with nothing to be done about it
>> step.1: stir, stand 10 min
>> step.2: mix to a rough dough
>> step.3: knead in 10 min
>> step.4: cover, rise until doubled
>> step.5: shape into a log, proof in a 9x5-in loaf pan
>> step.6: brush, bake 350°F 35 min

Stir @whole milk{1 1/4%cup}(300 mL; warmed to 110°F) with @granulated sugar{2%Tbs}(25 g) and @instant yeast{2 1/4%tsp}(7 g), then let stand ~{10%min}.

Add @bread flour{3 3/4%cup}(500 g) and @table salt{2%tsp}(12 g) to @&(~1)yeast mixture{}.

Knead @softened unsalted butter{4%Tbs}(55 g) into @&(~1)dough{} for ~{10%min}.

Cover @&(~1)dough{} and rise until doubled, ~{1%hour}.

Shape @&(~1)dough{} into a log and proof in a #9x5-in loaf pan{} until crowned, ~{1%hour}.

Brush @&(~1)loaf{} with @melted butter{1%Tbs} and bake at 350°F for ~{35%min}.
